# S0: the dress rehearsal of session a (2026-10-07, ADR-0144): every stage 0 to
# 14 once, end to end, on the grid run_campaign.py derives from the registered
# session (REHEARSAL_N below) before the registered S1 run. Campaign slug `smoke`.
EXP=S0
SESSION=a
CAMPAIGN=smoke
# The anchor model: cache_budget's MODEL_KV registers qwen3-14b, llama-3.3-70b,
# deepseek-v3 and qwen3-next-80b only (review 2026-10-06, HIGH 3).
MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-14B
MODEL_SLUG=qwen3-14b
GPU_ID="NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3"
GPU_COUNT=1
# Datacenter fallbacks (2026-10-07 16:49 UTC: US-NE-1 and US-CA-2 had no H100
# stock; stock listed in CA-MTL-1, EU-FR-1, EUR-IS-3, AP-JP-1, AP-IN-1, AP-IN-2).
# Same GPU and secure price everywhere; the volume is created beside the pod.
DC_PREFS="US-NE-1 US-CA-2 CA-MTL-1 EU-FR-1 EUR-IS-3 AP-JP-1 AP-IN-1 AP-IN-2"
ENGINES="vllm sglang"
# Review 2026-10-13 A4: SGLang ladders first (its 254 s relaunches and the
# fp8 and FA3 questions surface in the first ladder, not the second).
CALIBRATE="sglang vllm"
TOPOLOGY=single
# The rehearsal at n = 50: 110 cells, 110 windows, 38 relaunches, 23 dry
# windows [V offline plan 2026-10-09, ADR-0152/0153/0155]. ADR-0162: attempt 1
# (2026-10-08) hit the 6 h bound with the run still going: 106 windows took
# 8.79 h, 2.97 h of windows and 5.82 h of per-invocation preparation (CPU
# retrieval, reranking, warm-up; mean 198 s) [V cell.json]. HOURS bounds the
# run job. S0F-88 B-5 (owner ruling R9, 2026-10-12): attempt 4's run took
# 35,639 s, 99 percent of the 10 h bound, with 31 cells not run; the measured
# step table (run_campaign.RUN_*_SECONDS) projects the same plan with every
# cell run at 11.74 h [V]. The S0F-88 audit then added 100 measured
# arrivals per pressure window after a 30 s pre-load (owner decision
# 2026-10-12, U3): the same plan projects 15.67 h (the 50-query step times
# scaled linearly plus the pre-load) [V offline plan]. 17 h keeps the 1.2 h
# spare. The rerank rows are CPU times and the scaling counts fixed costs
# twice: an upper bound [D].
HOURS=17
# seatbelt >= setup 25 + load gate 10 + pod suite 30 + validate 2x25 + calibrate
# 2x60 + calibrate-rungs 2x720 (S0F-88: every class laddered, 12 h per engine)
# + plan 15 + run 1,020 + score 300 + collect 30 + pull 60 = 3,100 min (51.7 h).
# Review 2026-10-13 item 6: 60h leaves about 8 h for provision, ship, seal,
# polling and an overnight stop at stage 8 (the bounds left 20 min at 50h).
SEATBELT=60h
# Review 2026-10-13 item 6: 1,600 RULER rows at about 5.1 s each is about
# 2.3 h of scoring against the 180 min default.
SCORE_BOUND_MIN=300
# Review 2026-10-13 item 5: a compression-arm cell prepares hundreds of
# requests on the CPU before its clock (U6), which the monitor read as an idle
# cell at 30 min (20 HARD alerts on attempt 4).
CELL_STALL_MIN=60
# Review 2026-10-13 item 17: tar archives of the run tree on the network volume
BACKUP_ARCHIVE_DIR=/workspace/backup-archives
# S0F-88 U3: the pressure (window) cells measure 100 arrivals, so the qasper
# manifest must give 100 ids per trial (built offline 2026-10-12 from the
# cached split: 75 blocks, pool 303, trials disjoint); squad_v2 serves F1 at 50.
QUERY_MANIFESTS="squad_v2=data/manifests/squad_v2_50x3_seed42.json qasper=data/manifests/qasper_100x3_seed42.json"
PREFETCH_MODELS="Qwen/Qwen3-14B intfloat/e5-large-v2 BAAI/bge-reranker-large microsoft/llmlingua-2-xlm-roberta-large-meetingbank KRLabsOrg/lettucedect-base-modernbert-en-v1 MoritzLaurer/DeBERTa-v3-base-mnli-fever-anli sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 roberta-base"
# ADR-0144: the rehearsal grid (see _common.env) and the consent to skip the
# registered-but-blocked cells loudly (B8 retr-store on sglang: no connector
# knob on that launcher; 3 cells of session a).
REHEARSAL_N=50
SKIP_BLOCKED=1
# Decision 3 (2026-10-13): S0 is design input; a partial tree is sealed,
# scored and analyzed (attempt 4 had 14 failed dry windows and still scored).
PARTIAL_TREE_OK=1
# Review 2026-10-13, Part 8 bundle (owner approved): stop a ladder at its first
# failed rung; bound every step at 1.5 h (the longest honest step on attempt 4
# was a rerank cell at about 11 min, a compression prep about 35 min); rerun a
# dry window whose telemetry was refused once (decision 10).
LADDER_FAIL_FAST=1
STEP_TIMEOUT_S=5400
DRY_TELEMETRY_RERUN=1
FRONT_LOAD=1
RUN_FAIL_FAST=infra
# S0F-57 / ADR-0158: the rehearsal has executable vLLM retr-store (B8) cells
# (stage 0: NEEDS_LMCACHE=1); the bootstrap installs the connector package and
# the rehearsal is the live test of the LMCache <-> vLLM 0.19.1 pairing.
INSTALL_LMCACHE=1
# Planner inputs of the S0 day 2026-09-30 (S0_RUN_2026-09-30.md section 3:
# c = 50, s = 3,100 chosen and recorded; 77,500 KV tokens at r = 0.5). The
# _common.env placeholders (8, 2048) give a KV pool under the 32K request cap
# at every r <= 1.5 and vLLM refuses to start. The service time stays [A].
FLOOR_CONCURRENCY=50
# ADR-0155: the anchor arm's served shape (gold-fresh, 4,779 tokens on the
# 2026-10-08 landing), never the 3,100 of the 2026-09-30 note; the plan refuses
# a floor table sized on another shape. The rehearsal calibrates 3 rungs per
# engine (0.75, 1.25 from the collapsed F2, 0.5 from F3) on two classes
# (ADR-0156): about 4 h per engine at the measured probe durations (ADR-0162;
# the 90 min figure assumed 85 s windows), bound CALIBRATE_RUNGS_BOUND_S.
FLOOR_AVG_SEQ_TOKENS=4779
# S0F-88 B-9 (owner ruling R5, 2026-10-12): the rehearsal ladders EVERY demand
# class at its own pressure rungs (calibrate-rungs --all-classes), because the
# two-anchor interpolation missed mid classes by 10 to 29 percent on S0
# attempt 4; S1 picks its method from this run's measured interpolation error.
# Expected per engine with the GPU reranker (B-6): anchor about 40 min,
# smallest about 70 min, six mid classes about 2.5 h, about 4.3 h in all [D
# from the attempt 4 window spans, A: about 2.75 min per window once the CPU
# rerank leaves the window]. The independent review of 2026-10-12 simulated
# the per-class ladders at 129 to 136 windows per engine, about 6 to 8 h [D];
# the owner set the bound to 12 h per engine (2026-10-12, "raise to 12hrs").
RUNG_ALL_CLASSES=1
CALIBRATE_RUNGS_BOUND_S=43200
# SUITE_ON_POD=1 IS built: stage 4 runs the full suite as a pod job (30 min
# bound) before the engine validation. The refusal controls and the pd probes
# are not built into the validate stage yet: stage 4 refuses when either is 1
# (visible, never silent). Owner's default 6 of 2026-10-06 folds them in as
# tracked code later.
SUITE_ON_POD=1
NEGATIVE_CONTROLS=0
PD_PROBES=0
# MAC_SUITE=0 (owner, 2026-10-07 16:20 UTC, ADR-0145): the full Mac suite passed
# on HEAD fd501cc at 16:00 UTC (4,321 passed, 36 skipped; the one failure was the
# fake-job status race in test_run_exit_2_with_stop_failed_only_is_accepted_and_noted,
# which passed in the three other runs of the day); SUITE_ON_POD=1 above keeps
# the suite on the pod as the gate of this rehearsal.
MAC_SUITE=0
# S0F-35 (live H100 CA-MTL-1, 2026-10-07 17:50 UTC, pod 68bqg4rw7w86tu): SGLang
# 0.5.10.post1 died in its piecewise CUDA-graph capture of Qwen3-14B
# ("FusedAddRMSNorm failed ... an illegal memory access"); SGLang's own log
# names the workaround. The master forwards this lever to the engine jobs.
CAGE_SGLANG_DISABLE_PIECEWISE_CUDA_GRAPH=1
# S0F-39 (live CA-MTL-1, 2026-10-07 19:59 UTC): the network volume (NFS4, vast
# backend) refuses "|" in file names and every cell directory is its row key,
# so the results root and the backup live on the container disk for this
# rehearsal (pulled to the Mac at stage 12; the pod's disk is not durable).
POD_RESULTS_DIR=/root/cage-results
POD_BACKUP_DIR=/root/backup
BACKUP_TARGET=file:///root/backup
